# Test: a replay flood of one already-admitted PADR, from one MAC, leaves the
# AC's own open-file-descriptor count flat, and the AC keeps answering PADI
# afterward.
#
# VALIDATES: 10000 replays of a captured, valid PADR from one MAC allocate at
#            most one session's worth of descriptors (process_open_fds on the
#            AC's own Prometheus endpoint), because matchLiveCookie
#            (session.go) answers a replayed cookie in every live session
#            state, not only StateDiscovery (server.go, handlePADR)
# VALIDATES: the AC answers a fresh PADI with a PADO after the flood, so the
#            flood does not wedge or exhaust the discovery path
# PREVENTS: the AC that this spec exists to fix -- one host on an access
#           interface exhausting the AC's file descriptors by replaying a
#           single valid PADR. Before the dedup branch covered every live
#           session state, each replay past the first re-entered the
#           allocation path (a fresh session ID, AF_PPPOX socket, /dev/ppp
#           channel and unit), so this test's descriptor-growth assertion
#           went red against the pre-fix code
#           (spec-pppoe-padr-replay-allocates-unbounded-sessions, AC-6).
#
# max-sessions-per-mac is left at its default (8): AC-6 is the dedup branch
# holding under a replay flood, not the cap. A flood of 10000 replays of the
# SAME cookie is entirely absorbed by matchLiveCookie before admitPerMACCap
# is ever consulted, so this test would pass even with the cap effectively
# disabled -- pppoe-per-mac-cap.ci is what proves the cap itself refuses.
#
# No http=wait readiness barrier precedes the foreground command below: HTTP
# checks in this format run only after every cmd= directive has finished
# (ci-format.md, "HTTP Checks"), so a wait placed before cmd=foreground would
# not run any earlier than one placed after it. The fixture itself polls
# /metrics for its baseline read (tunnelPPPoEProcessOpenFDs).
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=netns-link:name=veth-bng:peer=veth-sub


stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
pppoe {
    enabled true
    ac-name ze-test
    interface veth-bng {
    }
}

telemetry {
    prometheus {
        enabled true
        server main {
            ip 127.0.0.1
            port $PORT2
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.pppoe:value=debug
option=env:var=TEST_IFACE:value=veth-sub

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture pppoe/padr-flood $PORT2:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: initial session admitted, session-id=
expect=stdout:contains=OK: process_open_fds grew by at most one session's worth after 10000 PADR replays
expect=stdout:contains=OK: the AC answered a new PADI after the flood
